from ./Components import Components
from ./Compositions import Compositions
from ./Config import Config
from ./Escapes import Escapes
from ./Fonts import Fonts
from ./Layout import Layout
from ./Modules import Modules
from ./Values import Values
from ./componentProperties/html/HtmlTag import HtmlTag

export anchor Errors:
    description:
        What the Emul compiler reports when a source file is wrong, or
        probably not what its author meant. Problems are either errors or
        warnings.

    severity:
        - errors
            The source can't be compiled as written. When there is any error,
            nothing is rendered.
        - warnings
            The source compiles and renders, but something in it is likely a
            mistake, or has no effect.

    reporting:
        Each problem is reported with its severity, the file, line and column
        it was found at, a message, and a short code in square brackets. The
        offending line is shown beneath it, with the problem marked. All
        problems in a project are reported together, rather than stopping at
        the first.

        ```text
        \\\
        error: designs/Buttons.emul:4:5: `colour` is not a property [unknown-property]
          4 |     colour: #dc2626
            |     ^^^^^^
        \\\
        ```

    syntaxErrors:
        - unexpected-indentation
            A line is indented where no component is open, or indented
            inconsistently within one.
        - unclosed-brace
            A composition or instance body is opened and never closed.
        - unexpected-brace
            A closing brace has no matching opening brace, or text follows the
            closing brace of a composition on the same line.
        - unexpected-character
            A composition body holds something that is not quoted text, an
            attribute, an instance or a comment.
        - unclosed-quote
            Quoted text or a quoted value is not closed before the end of the
            line.
        - unclosed-escape
            An escape wrapper, as described in @{Escapes}, is opened and never
            closed, or is closed with a different number of backslashes.
        - missing-colon
            A component declaration or property line has no colon.
        - unknown-keyword
            A top-level line starts with something other than `component`,
            `composition`, `export`, `from`, or a comment.
        - mixed-indentation
            A file indents with tabs in some places and spaces in others, or
            with different numbers of spaces per level.
        - invalid-name
            A component or composition name is not PascalCase, meaning a
            capital letter followed by letters and digits only.
        - missing-body
            An instance's name is not followed by a body in braces. An
            instance with nothing in it is still written with empty braces.

    componentErrors:
        - unknown-property
            A property is not one of those listed in @{Components}.
        - invalid-value
            A value is not one the property accepts, as set out in its own
            entry and in @{Values}. This includes a unit other than `px` or
            `%` for a size, a percentage where the property takes only `px`, a
            negative value where it is not allowed, an unknown keyword, and a
            colour in a format Emul does not accept.
        - duplicate-property
            A component sets the same property more than once.
        - empty-value
            A property line has nothing after its colon.
        - content-in-component
            A component contains text, an instance, or anything else that
            is not a property line.
        - invalid-html-tag
            An @{HtmlTag} value is not a lowercase element name, or is one of
            the tags that are not allowed.

    inheritanceErrors:
        - unknown-component
            A component extends, or a composition instances, a name that is
            not a component declared in the same file or imported into it.
        - extends-cycle
            A component extends itself, directly or through other components.
        - extends-composition
            A component extends a composition.

    compositionErrors:
        - instance-of-composition
            An instance names a composition rather than a component.
            Compositions can't be placed inside one another.
        - content-in-root
            The root of a composition holds text or attributes. The root holds
            instances only.
        - content-in-void-element
            An instance whose component has a void htmlTag, such as `img`,
            has text or children.
        - block-in-inline
            An instance whose component is `display: inline` has a child that
            is not inline. Inline instances hold only text and other inline
            instances, as described in @{Layout}.
        - missing-src
            An instance whose component has the htmlTag `img` has no `src`
            attribute.
        - duplicate-attribute
            An instance sets the same attribute more than once.
        - style-attribute
            An attribute's name is the identifier of a component property,
            such as `color`. Styling belongs in components, not instances.
        - reserved-attribute
            An attribute is named `class` or `style`. Emul sets both itself.
        - invalid-attribute-name
            An attribute's name is not lowercase letters, digits and hyphens,
            starting with a letter.
        - missing-image
            A `src` attribute or an image `url()` points at a file that does
            not exist, or at a remote URL.
        - unsupported-image
            An image file is not PNG, JPEG, WebP or SVG, or can't be read.

    moduleErrors:
        - duplicate-name
            Two declarations or imports in one file have the same name.
            Components and compositions share one set of names.
        - missing-file
            An import path does not point at an existing file or module.
        - not-exported
            An import names something the other file does not export, or does
            not declare at all.
        - export-unknown
            An `export` line, or a `from ... export` line, names something
            that does not exist.

    fontErrors:
        - unknown-font-family
            A fontFamily names a family that Google Fonts does not have.
        - missing-font-face
            A component uses a fontWeight or fontStyle that its family does
            not offer. Emul never fakes one, as described in @{Fonts}.
        - font-unavailable
            A font file is not in the cache and can't be downloaded, such as
            when building offline for the first time.

    outputErrors:
        - invalid-size
            A width or height, in the config or on the command line, is not a
            whole number from 1 to 16384, or a scale is not a positive number.
        - output-too-large
            A PNG would be over 16384 pixels on either side after scaling.

    configErrors:
        - invalid-config
            The `emul.config.pi` file does not compile as Piton, or does not
            export exactly one `emul-config` anchor.
        - missing-entry
            The entry file set in @{Config}, or the default one, does not
            exist.
        - unknown-format
            The formats setting lists something other than `html`, `svg` and
            `png`.
        - invalid-setting
            A config setting has a value of the wrong kind, such as an
            svgFonts value other than `outline` or `embed`, or a size entry
            for a composition that does not exist.

    warnings:
        - no-effect
            A property can't have any effect where the component is used. For
            example, `gap` on a component whose display is not flex or grid,
            `flexGrow` on an instance whose parent is not a flex container,
            `top` on a component whose position is `static`, or `padding` on
            an inline component.
        - percentage-height-ignored
            A percentage height is used where the parent's height is `auto`,
            so it is treated as `auto`, as described in @{Layout}.
        - empty-composition
            A composition has nothing in its root, so it renders an empty
            canvas.
        - unused-declaration
            A component or composition that is not exported is never used in
            its own file.
        - unused-import
            An imported name is never used.
        - duplicate-extends
            A component lists the same component more than once after
            `extends`.
        - shorthand-overlap
            A component sets both a shorthand and a specific property it
            covers. The specific one wins, as described in @{Components}, but
            the overlap is often a leftover.
        - nothing-to-render
            The entry file exports no compositions, so nothing is rendered.
        - not-rendered
            A composition is exported from a file other than the entry, and
            is not exported from the entry either, so it is never rendered.

    notErrors:
        Some things look wrong but are allowed:

        - circular imports, as described in @{Modules}
        - a `//` partway through a line, which is part of the value, not a
            comment
        - an instance with an empty body, such as a divider drawn only by its
            component's styling
        - a component that is exported but never used, since another project
            may use it

    compositionsLink:
        The rules for bodies, text and attributes that these errors enforce
        are described in @{Compositions}.
